gin runs 7pp above the Technology median (7%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","It earns less of the sector's profit than its revenue share would suggest (0.61x).","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-1.0% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 533 companies in the universe; the top four hold 29% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 51% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 24% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 46% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 71% and a beta of 1.41, it amplifies market moves.","About $40.6M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 53% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 97% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $102 (margin of safety -3%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 23%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $65.55 to $164 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Technology peers: EV/EBITDA 28.8 vs 17.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 67% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.3% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $132 on average, 26% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 46% clears the cost of capital of 11.4% by 35pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.19).","It runs a 41% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 13.0% of revenue on R&D and 2.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $304.4M."